From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:42:08 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] vb-screen

The Virtual Boy gets its own Screen section, listed last and shown
only when the card holds Virtual Boy games, with five rows. Shader walks
Off and the retro list, stored in Config/vb_shader.txt. Picture is
Actual by default (the 384x224 picture at 1.875x, 720x420 with a band
above and below) or Stretch (the whole panel), stored as vb in
Config/picture.txt. VB Speed is the Native or Panel row of ADR 0071:
Beetle VB reports 50.27 fps, and Native paces it at its own rate.

Palette is the core's eight vb_color_mode choices, black and red first
(the hardware's LEDs), then white, blue, cyan, electric cyan, green,
magenta and yellow. Right Pad is Stick (the right analog stick is the
second D-pad) or ABXY (patch vb-input). Both live in Config/vb.txt, the
factory choice is red and the stick, the user's choice becomes the
default and applies from the next game. A missing line is the factory
choice and an unknown one is logged and read as it.
